or GATA-2 in urogenital development</article-title><source><italic>The EMBO Journal</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>17</volume><issue>22</issue><fpage>6689</fpage><lpage>6700</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9822612</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Challen</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Identifying the molecular phenotype of renal progenitor cells</article-title><source><italic>Journal of the American Society of Nephrology</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>15</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>2344</fpage><lpage>2357</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15339983</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>NCBI Pubmed</collab><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi">http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi</ext-link>.</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zadeh</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanavoli</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Haines</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kreutzer</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Despite large-scale T cell activation, only a minor subset of T cells       responding <italic>in vitro</italic> to <italic>Actinobacillus actinomycetemcomitans</italic>      differentiate into effector T cells</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Periodontal Research</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>35</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>136</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10929867</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="gov"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ghahramani</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Hinton</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parameter estimation for linear dynamical systems</article-title><year>1996</year><publisher-loc>Toronto, Ontario, Canada</publisher-loc><publisher-name>University of Toronto</publisher-name><comment>Tech. Rep..</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shumway</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Stoffer</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><source><italic>Time Series Analysis and Applications</italic></source><year>2000</year><publisher-loc>New York, NY, USA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Springer</publisher-name><series>Springer Texts in Statistics</series></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Effron</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><source><italic>An Introduction to the Bootstrap</italic></source><year>1993</year><publisher-loc>New York, NY, USA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Chapman &#x00026; Hall/CRC</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dougherty</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Coefficient of determination in nonlinear signal processing</article-title><source><italic>Signal Processing</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>80</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>2219</fpage><lpage>2235</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><labe